{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2211 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "4b5c1b7c192f53187708aa994cf3522cc68d8faa22ef5551c53e6b1c74fb6854" :edb/db-before-t 2210 :edb/db-after-t 2211 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535523 50 #inst "2026-10-09T01:45:49.668Z" 13194139535523 true] [17592186064082 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353614 13194139535523 true] [17592186353614 1017 #edb/ref 17592186353615 13194139535523 true] [17592186353614 1089 "q-22084" 13194139535523 true] [17592186353614 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535523 true] [17592186353614 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4/3}-24{x}^{1/3}-6{x}^{-2/3}$ defined on $(0,\\infty ).$ Given that ${f}^{′}(1)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(1)=0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=1$" 13194139535523 true] [17592186353614 1113 #uuid "648e472e-d530-5d5d-b8f5-fb9004bc624e" 13194139535523 true] [17592186353614 1145 "We're given that $x=1$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4/3}-24{x}^{1/3}-6{x}^{-2/3},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4{x}^{1/3}-8{x}^{-2/3}+4{x}^{-5/3}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{-2/3}+\\frac{16}{3}{x}^{-5/3}-\\frac{20}{3}{x}^{-8/3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1) & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot (1)^{-2/3}+\\frac{16}{3}\\cdot (1)^{-5/3}-\\frac{20}{3}\\cdot (1)^{-8/3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is zero, we conclude that the test is inconclusive, we need to use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's  find the stationary points. These points are the solution of the equation ${f}^{′}(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{1/3}-8{x}^{-2/3}+4{x}^{-5/3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{-5/3}(4{x}^{2}-8x+4) & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{-5/3}{(x-1)}^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the only stationary point on $(0,\\infty )$ is $x=1.$\n\nLet's choose auxiliary points from each side of the stationary point and evaluate the first derivative at them. We take the auxiliary points $x=\\frac{1}{2},2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}) & =4{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-5/3}{(\\frac{1}{2}-1)}^{2} \\\\  & =4{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-5/3}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{{2}^{-5/3}})(\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={2}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{5/3}\\cdot {2}^{-2} \\\\  & ={2}^{5/3}>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =4\\cdot {2}^{-5/3}(2-1)^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2-5/3} \\\\  & ={2}^{1/3}>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the first derivative does not change the sign at $x=1$, we conclude that $f(x)$ has no relative extrema at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139535523 true] [17592186353615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353616 13194139535523 true] [17592186353615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353617 13194139535523 true] [17592186353615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353618 13194139535523 true] [17592186353615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353619 13194139535523 true] [17592186353615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353620 13194139535523 true] [17592186353615 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535523 true] [17592186353615 1041 "selection" 13194139535523 true] [17592186353615 1104 #edb/ref 17592186353617 13194139535523 true] [17592186353615 1110 #uuid "b7b5b007-851a-5efc-b630-78d7a6b2737d" 13194139535523 true] [17592186353616 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535523 true] [17592186353616 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535523 true] [17592186353616 1111 #uuid "86bb8250-5f0c-5be3-b3a3-84ddbdb998e6" 13194139535523 true] [17592186353617 1034 "I only" 13194139535523 true] [17592186353617 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535523 true] [17592186353617 1111 #uuid "329c5b59-f1a8-5258-9cdc-ee0a08cb9158" 13194139535523 true] [17592186353618 1034 "III only" 13194139535523 true] [17592186353618 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535523 true] [17592186353618 1111 #uuid "a7edc25f-0337-5652-99b8-0a7ce55deec0" 13194139535523 true] [17592186353619 1034 "I 